        "general_completion": "; The sequence A228741 is the number of arrays of the median of three adjacent elements of some length-6 0..n array.\n; The median of three numbers a, b, c is (a+b+c)/3.\n; The Wiener index (also known as the shortest path sum) for a complete graph with n vertices is given by the formula n*(n-1)/2.\n; The number of arrays of the median of three adjacent elements of some length-6 0..n array is thus n*(n-1)/6.\n; This can be derived by considering each triplet of adjacent elements (a,b,c) in the array, and for each triplet, there are exactly 6 possible ways to choose the median (a, b, c, a+b, b+c, c+a).\n; Therefore, the number of such arrays is 6 times the number of triplets of adjacent elements in the array, which is n*(n-1)/6.\n\n; Let's implement this in a loop to compute the value for a given n.\n\nloop:\n    inc $2\n    mov $0,$2\n    mov $1,$0\n    div $1,$2\n    dec $2\n    cmp $2,",
